"pull" fetches the pull-request heads of each remote, but only those that are relevant to the
clone.  Pull request 1's head is a commit that the clone has.  Pull request 2's head is a commit
that the clone lacks, so it is not fetched.  Pull request 3's head is a commit that the clone lacks,
but an earlier pull fetched an earlier head of pull request 3.  The remote no longer has pull
request 4, so its ref is deleted.  Remote "other" has pull request 5, and is not on GitHub.
